An element ref written inside a callback resolves to the emitted node.

A program names a node with `#id`, and html does not reuse that name as a JS
variable: the id would have to survive JS scoping and could collide with a
reserved word or a global the page already emits, so the node comes out as
`$0` and the mapping is recorded in refToVar. The translator applies it
wherever a lowered node op names a ref -- and never reached inside a callback,
because the walk that dispatches those ops descended into a call's arguments
only for the two closures an offloaded blocking call leaves behind.

So `run(func() { … })` got nothing. A write to `#out` inside it kept the name
the program gave it, the page said `out.textContent = …`, and `out` is a name
nothing declares:

    THREW: out is not defined

The whole page died at that point -- not the callback, the script. And no event
is needed to reach it: the fixture below is a bare user function taking a
callback.

The gate is gone rather than widened, which is what makes it general: any
argument may be a callback, an assignment may hold one
(`handle = setInterval(func() { … })`, which is how html schedules), and a
local's initialiser may too. isAsyncOffloadCall existed only to name the
special case and is deleted with it.

The walk stops at the outermost callback, since WalkLowered on its block
reaches whatever nests below, and copies rather than rewriting in place --
walking one body twice nests the translation inside itself, which is the
warning walkComponentProps already carries.

deny out/none/html/index.html `\bout\.textContent` -- the ref resolves to the emitted variable, never to the written id

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"
import app "sngl:app"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

func run(f func()) {
    f()
}

component main ui {
    var n = 0

    effect(@mount {
        run(func() {
            n += 1
        })
    })
    text #out(value="{n}")
}

app.window {
    main
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
<!-- Code generated by sngl (html) from app.sngl; DO NOT EDIT. -->

